# No PKI material — public or private — is committed to git. The CA, certs, keys,
# and CSRs all live under secrets/ (below) on shared storage and are distributed
# by the signing workflow (README §6 Phase 6 / §9), never through the repo.
secrets/**
!secrets/
!secrets/**/
!secrets/**/.gitkeep

# Backstop: never commit key/cert material dropped anywhere under mesh/, even
# outside secrets/. Extensions are ambiguous (a .pem may hold a private key), so
# the guard is deliberately broad; anything that must persist belongs in secrets/.
*.key
*_key
*.pem
*.crt
*.csr
*.pub
*.pfx
*.p12
*.p8
*.der
*.p7b
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# e2e-generated throwaway PKI (created by mesh/tests/e2e-up.sh, never real)
tests/.e2e-pki/

# node-host settings for compose.node.yml (copied from node.env.example) —
# host-specific, never shared through the repo
.env
*.env
!node.env.example
